TITLE:: RCVisuals
summary:: sound data from a song to HomewareVisuals
categories:: Libraries>reCurrent
related:: Classes/RCOrgnsm, Classes/RCOsc, Classes/SendReply

DESCRIPTION::
The link between a reCurrent song and HomewareVisuals (SuperCollider → OSC/UDP 57300 → bridge → WebSocket → a page). One address, sends that land when the sound does, and the two hooks a rig needs to describe its sounds: a per-event key for orgnsm templates and a relay of server replies (link::Classes/SendReply::) to the page.

code::
RCVisuals.send('/orgnsm/gone', 12);                                   // now
RCVisuals.sendForEvent(ev, '/orgnsm/note', [12, 440, 0.1]);           // when the event's sound starts
tpl.attrDictBase = tpl.attrDictBase ++ [viz: RCVisuals.notePfunc('/orgnsm/note', { |ev| [ev.freq, ev.amp] })];
RCVisuals.relay(\plankton, '/plankton/viz', '/orgnsm/state', ~server);   // [replyID, values...] forwarded
::

A delayed send goes on SystemClock from the calling thread's logical time: a Pfunc evaluated at an event's logical time sends at that time plus the server latency, when the sound starts. code::enabled = false:: sends nothing (a gig without visuals); code::sink:: replaces the network by a Function code::{ |path, args| }:: (tests, offline checks).

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: setAddr
The bridge address (default 127.0.0.1 and link::#*defaultPort::, far from the ports sclang takes for itself from 57120 up; 57121 until Oct 24 2026).
argument:: hostarg
argument:: portarg
The port; nil: link::#*defaultPort::.
returns:: the link::Classes/NetAddr::

METHOD:: defaultPort
The port when none is named: the environment's code::RC_VISUALS_PORT:: when set, else 57300, the bridge of the user's stack (HomewareVisuals' main checkout), which the IDE reaches. HomewareSC's headless runs (its code::scripts/lib.sh:: code::run_sclang::) set it to their checkout's own bridge (a paired HomewareVisuals worktree's) or to 57399, which nothing binds, so a check or a probe never draws on the pages the user has open; its rig's live side sets it to the bridge it means to feed. A script that should reach a bridge names it: code::RCVisuals.setAddr("127.0.0.1", port)::, as HomewareVisuals' demos do with their checkout's port.

METHOD:: addr
The NetAddr messages go to.

METHOD:: send
Send now.
argument:: path
argument::  ... args
returns:: true when a message went out (or into the sink)

METHOD:: sendArgs
code::send:: with the args as one Array.

METHOD:: sendIn
Send in code::delay:: seconds of the calling thread's logical time (SystemClock); at once when the delay is nil or not positive.
argument:: delay
argument:: path
argument:: args

METHOD:: ctl
A value for the reprocessing of a take's video: code::'/fx/ctl' <name> <value>:: sent in code::delay:: seconds (the default server's latency), when the sound it goes with starts. HomewareVisuals' effects page maps it onto an effect's parameter (code::/fx/map::); in a take rendered offline it lands in the tape, which HomewareSC's code::take.sh render --viz:: sets apart as the take's control tape (link::Guides/reCording#Reprocessing::).
argument:: name
argument:: value
argument:: delay

METHOD:: sendForEvent
Send when the event's sound starts: after code::eventDelay(ev)::.
argument:: ev
argument:: path
argument:: args

METHOD:: eventDelay
Seconds between an event's logical time and its sound: the server latency (the event's own code::\latency:: when set), its code::\lag::, its code::\timingOffset:: (beats of the beat's clock). The server is the beat's layer's, else the event's, else the default.
argument:: ev

METHOD:: notePfunc
A value for an orgnsm's attrDict: at every non-rest event, code::func.(ev):: gives the args sent to code::path:: when the sound starts (nil: nothing). Put it after the keys it reads (code::freq::, code::amp::...): keys are computed in order. The key's own value is 0 and never reaches a synth (only a def's control names are sent). A failing function is reported under the code::\visuals:: tag, not thrown.
argument:: path
argument:: func

METHOD:: relay
Server replies (link::Classes/SendReply::, link::Classes/SendTrig::: code::[cmd, nodeID, replyID, values...]::) arriving on code::replyPath:: are forwarded to code::outPath:: as code::argFunc.(msg):: (default code::[replyID, values...]::; nil sends nothing). One relay per key; permanent (Cmd-. keeps it).
argument:: key
argument:: replyPath
argument:: outPath
argument:: server
argument:: argFunc
returns:: the link::Classes/OSCFunc::

METHOD:: unrelay
returns:: true when a relay of that key was freed

METHOD:: freeRelays

METHOD:: relayKeys

METHOD:: enabled
false: nothing is sent (default true).

METHOD:: sink
A Function code::{ |path, args| }:: that replaces the network (tests, offline checks); nil sends over UDP. A take rendered offline records what passes here, with the offline clock's seconds, as its visuals tape (link::Classes/REVisualsTape::); what a relay would forward from the server (the taps' positions and levels) comes out of a render through link::Classes/REOfflineTap:: instead, since NRT answers no reply.

METHOD:: sent
Messages sent (or sunk) since code::resetCount::.

METHOD:: resetCount
